  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe machine page pushed its action row (\"Load other\", \"Edit\", \"Clear\")\nbelow the visible bottom of a 720 px window. The bottom 40 px band of\nthe Properties pane holds the separator and the `Close` footer, and the\npage's `ScrollArea` ends above it (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs`).\nThe buttons sat in that band, so the user had to scroll to reach them.\n\nTwo commits fix this:\n\n1. `test(ui)`: the pinning test now measures each button bottom against\n   the top of the `Close` footer - the page's visible bottom - not the\n   bottom of the Properties leaf. This test was red on the previous\n   head with the reviewer's exact numbers (buttons 644..668, `Close`\n   top 648).\n2. `fix(ui)`: the page reclaims the row. `Refresh` shares the `Library`\n   combo row (right-to-left, so the combo cannot push it out). The page\n   uses a 2 px row rhythm (the overview grid takes a `row_gap`\n   parameter; the machine editor keeps its 4 px). The two ownership\n   help lines are drawn small and weak: each drops from about 45 px to\n   20 px. No AccessKit label, word or command changed.\n\nMeasured in `shell_harness()` at 1280x720: the action row moved from\n644..668 (inside the `Close` band) to 570..594, above the `Close` top\nat 648. No scrolling needed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nMachine page, Setup1 with the Tormach 770MX, window client 1280x720.\n\nBefore: the action row falls under the fold, behind the `Close` footer.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-2105/2105-before.png)\n\nAfter: the whole page, including \"Load other\", \"Edit\" and \"Clear\",\nstands above the `Close` footer without scrolling.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-2105/2105-after.png)\n\n## Readings\n\n- Review finding reproduced: at the previous head the buttons' bottoms\n  (668) sat below the ScrollArea bottom (about 642), in the `Close`\n  band (648..666).\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2105-machine-buttons-720.md`, with\n  the measured y-values. It earlier named a button \"New\": that button\n  does not exist; the second commit corrects the text.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `the_machine_page_buttons_fit_without_scrolling_at_720_px`\n  (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/machine_page.rs`): red on the previous\n  head (the assertion panic names the `Close` edge), green at this\n  head.\n- `layout_page_setup_machine` (this page's named layout test): green,\n  still asserts `Refresh` right of the `Library` combo.\n\n## Gate\n\nQuick gate on the final head `b810c98a7`, `camcraft-ui` lib: 1249\npassed, 4 failed - only the four `frame_cost` tests that are red on\nmain too (#2766). Clippy `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: 0 warnings.\nVerified by hand in the built GUI at 1280x720 (after screenshot\nabove).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows narrower than 1280 px: the right-to-left row keeps `Refresh`\n  visible, but I did not test a narrower panel.\n- The other setup pages: `setup_pages.rs` draws the two ownership help\n  lines small and weak on the machine page path only; the machine\n  editor keeps its 4 px grid gap.\n\nChangelog: The machine page button row now fits a 720 px window: the\nRefresh button shares the machine library row.\n\nFixes #2105\n",
